            <ArticleTitle>Experimental study of the effects of Dietressa, a new weight-reducing drug.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>321-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The capacity of a new drug containing ultra-low doses of antibodies to cannabinoid receptor type 1 (Dietressa) to reduce body weight gain in mice on a high-calorie diet was evaluated, possible mechanisms of drug action were analyzed, and its safety (abuse potential in the reaction of self-stimulation) was evaluated. Dietressa was not inferior to sibutramine in reducing body weight gain in mice and exhibited no abuse potential.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
